IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `srcr-rules`

-- Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019 (Cth) -- the questions of the injured employee (the claimant)
-- in the Comcare scheme: an employee of the Commonwealth, a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019",
-- Compilation No. 2 (1 April 2024), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts only. Judgments the Act leaves to the determining authority (whether firefighting
-- duties were "not insubstantial", "unless the contrary is established", what is "reasonable and necessary") are asked
-- as facts or left with the authority; nothing here decides them.

§ `Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019 -- my questions as a claimant`

§§ `My employer and my treatment (ss 6, 7)`

@export Is my employer one of the bodies the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019 prescribe as an "Entity" under the Comcare scheme, and who is its principal officer (reg s 6, Schedule 2)? Other employers may still be Entities as Agencies or Parliamentary Departments; that is not answered here.
GIVEN `my employer` IS A `My employer` @desc Which body employs you? Choose "another employer" if it is not one of the seven listed.
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Who is the principal officer of my employer under the Regulations?` `my employer` MEANS
    `Schedule 2 -- the principal officer of my employer` `my employer`

@export Is my employer prescribed as an "Entity" by the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Regulations 2019 (reg s 6, Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my employer` IS A `My employer` @desc Which body employs you? Choose "another employer" if it is not one of the seven listed.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my employer a prescribed Entity?` `my employer` MEANS
    `s 6 -- my employer is a prescribed Entity` `my employer`

@export Does the Comcare scheme count my treatment by an occupational therapist, optometrist, podiatrist, psychologist or speech therapist as "medical treatment" I can claim for (reg s 7, Act s 4(1) paragraph (i))? Not answered for other practitioners, whom the Act's own paragraphs may cover.
GIVEN `my practitioner` IS A `Kind of practitioner` @desc What kind of practitioner treats you?
      `the treatment is therapeutic and given by or under the supervision of that practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it therapeutic treatment given by the practitioner, or under their supervision?
      `there is a national registration authority for the profession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a national registration authority for the practitioner's profession (within the meaning of section 8 of the Healthcare Identifiers Act 2010; for example a national board under the Health Practitioner Regulation National Law)?
      `the practitioner is registered by that authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the practitioner registered by that national registration authority?
      `the practitioner is a member of a relevant professional association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the practitioner a member of a relevant professional association (this counts only if there is no national registration authority)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my treatment prescribed medical treatment?` `my practitioner` `the treatment is therapeutic and given by or under the supervision of that practitioner` `there is a national registration authority for the profession` `the practitioner is registered by that authority` `the practitioner is a member of a relevant professional association` MEANS
    `s 7 -- the treatment is prescribed medical treatment`
        (`Treatment facts` WITH
            `practitioner` IS `my practitioner`
            `therapeutic treatment by or under the supervision of the practitioner` IS `the treatment is therapeutic and given by or under the supervision of that practitioner`
            `there is a national registration authority for the profession` IS `there is a national registration authority for the profession`
            `registered by that authority` IS `the practitioner is registered by that authority`
            `member of a relevant professional association` IS `the practitioner is a member of a relevant professional association`)

§§ `Firefighters' cancers (reg s 8A, Act s 7(8)) -- for an employee who was employed as a firefighter`

@export What qualifying period of firefighting employment does my cancer need before the Comcare scheme presumes my work caused it (Act s 7(8) table, reg s 8A)? The answer is in years; no answer means the disease is not in the table.
GIVEN `my disease` IS A `Disease` @desc Which disease do you suffer? Choose "another disease" if it is not listed.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`What qualifying period applies to my disease?` `my disease` MEANS
    `s 7(8) -- the qualifying period in years` `my disease`

@export I was employed as a firefighter: is my employment taken to have contributed, to a significant degree, to my cancer, unless the contrary is established (Act s 7(8), (9); reg ss 8A, 36)? No answer for a disease sustained before 4 July 2011 or a decision before 7 December 2011 (s 7(8) commenced on 7 December 2011; its application provision is not deposited). A yes is a presumption the determining authority can rebut; a no means only that s 7(8) does not help, not that the claim fails.
GIVEN `my disease` IS A `Disease` @desc Which disease do you suffer? Choose "another disease" if it is not listed.
      `years I was employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained` IS A NUMBER @desc How many years in all were you employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained? Add up separate periods (s 7(9)(b)). Count only periods in which firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of your duties.
      `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of my duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is (or was) the relevant authority deciding your claim satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of your duties in those years (s 7(9)(a))? This is the authority's judgement: answer as it stands, or ask the question both ways.
      `I was employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were those years of firefighting employment with the Commonwealth, a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation (s 7(9)(c))? Answer no if they were with another employer, such as a State fire service.
      `I was exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period?
      `the day the disease was sustained` IS A DATE @desc The day the disease was sustained: the day you first sought medical treatment for it, or the day it first caused incapacity for work or impairment, whichever came first (Act s 7(4)). ISO 8601, e.g. 2023-03-15.
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day the decision on your claim (or its reconsideration or review) is or was made. ISO 8601.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `my disease` `years I was employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained` `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of my duties` `I was employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation` `I was exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period` `the day the disease was sustained` `the day of the decision` MEANS
    `s 7(8) -- my employment is taken to have contributed to the disease`
        (`Firefighter facts` WITH
            `the disease` IS `my disease`
            `years employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained` IS `years I was employed as a firefighter before the disease was sustained`
            `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of the duties` IS `the relevant authority is satisfied that firefighting or related duties made up a not insubstantial portion of my duties`
            `employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation` IS `I was employed as a firefighter by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority or a licensed corporation`
            `exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period` IS `I was exposed to the hazards of a fire scene during that period`
            `the day the disease was sustained` IS `the day the disease was sustained`
            `the day of the decision` IS `the day of the decision`)

§§ `Indexing my normal weekly earnings each 1 July (regs ss 8-11, Act s 8(9B)-(9G)) -- for an employee receiving incapacity payments`

@export Which 1 July increase applies to my normal weekly earnings under the Comcare scheme: the one for employees who have left Commonwealth employment (Act s 8(9B), regs ss 8, 9), the one for earnings that have not otherwise changed in 12 months (Act s 8(9E), regs ss 10, 11), or both on the words of the Act?
GIVEN `I have ceased to be employed by the Commonwealth or a licensed corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you stopped being employed by the Commonwealth (including a Commonwealth authority) or the licensed corporation?
      `my normal weekly earnings were increased in the 12 months before this 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the 12 months before this 1 July, were your normal weekly earnings increased under s 8(6), (7) or (9) of the Act (for example because the pay for your class of employee rose while you were still employed)?
      `my normal weekly earnings were reduced in the 12 months before this 1 July` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the 12 months before this 1 July, were your normal weekly earnings reduced under s 8(9) of the Act?
GIVETH A `Which indexation`
`Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` `I have ceased to be employed by the Commonwealth or a licensed corporation` `my normal weekly earnings were increased in the 12 months before this 1 July` `my normal weekly earnings were reduced in the 12 months before this 1 July` MEANS
    `s 8(9B), (9E) -- the indexation that applies on 1 July` `I have ceased to be employed by the Commonwealth or a licensed corporation` `my normal weekly earnings were increased in the 12 months before this 1 July` `my normal weekly earnings were reduced in the 12 months before this 1 July`

@export I have stopped working for the Commonwealth or a licensed corporation: from what date are my normal weekly earnings first indexed (Act s 8(9C), reg s 5 "indexation date")? They are indexed again each 1 July after that.
GIVEN `the day my employment ceased` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment with the Commonwealth or the licensed corporation ceased. ISO 8601, e.g. 2025-03-31.
GIVETH A DATE
`When are my normal weekly earnings first indexed after I stopped working?` `the day my employment ceased` MEANS
    `s 8(9C) -- the first indexation date after I ceased` `the day my employment ceased`

@export By how many dollars a week do my normal weekly earnings go up on a 1 July indexation date, by the Wage Price Index (regs ss 9, 11)? The answer is 0 when the index has not risen.
GIVEN `my normal weekly earnings before the indexation date` IS A NUMBER @desc Your normal weekly earnings, in dollars a week, as they applied immediately before the indexation date (WE).
      `the index number for the December quarter of last year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Wage Price Index number (total hourly rates of pay excluding bonuses, all sectors, all Australia, original) for the quarter ended 31 December in the year before the indexation date, as published by the Australian Statistician.
      `the index number for the December quarter of the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc The same Wage Price Index number for the quarter ended 31 December a year earlier.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` `my normal weekly earnings before the indexation date` `the index number for the December quarter of last year` `the index number for the December quarter of the year before` MEANS
    `ss 9, 11 -- the further increase in dollars` `my normal weekly earnings before the indexation date` `the index number for the December quarter of last year` `the index number for the December quarter of the year before`

@export What is the indexation factor F for my normal weekly earnings this 1 July (regs ss 9, 11)? It is never less than 1.000.
GIVEN `the index number for the December quarter of last year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Wage Price Index number for the quarter ended 31 December in the year before the indexation date.
      `the index number for the December quarter of the year before` IS A NUMBER @desc The Wage Price Index number for the quarter ended 31 December a year earlier.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` `the index number for the December quarter of last year` `the index number for the December quarter of the year before` MEANS
    `ss 9, 11 -- F` `the index number for the December quarter of last year` `the index number for the December quarter of the year before`

§§ `How long Comcare or the licensee may take (reg s 11A, Act ss 61(1A), 62(6))`

@export By what day must my claim for compensation be determined (Act s 61(1A), reg s 11A(1))? 20 calendar days for an injury other than a disease, 60 for a disease, counting the day the claim was received, and not counting the days of any pause under reg s 11A(3). Claims made before 1 April 2024 have no prescribed period.
GIVEN `my claim is about` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc Is your claim about a disease (or the aggravation of a disease), or about another injury (or its aggravation)?
      `the day my claim was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the determining authority (Comcare or the licensee) received your claim. ISO 8601.
      `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim made in accordance with s 54 of the Act (in writing, in the approved form if one applies, given to the authority, with a medical certificate where required)?
      `the paused periods` IS A LIST OF `Paused period` @desc Each period, first and last day inclusive (ISO 8601), in which days are not counted (reg s 11A(3)): from the day you were given notice to attend a medical examination to the day the authority received the results; from the day you were asked for information or a document to the day the authority received it or you said you did not have it; from the day your employer was required to give information to the day the authority received it, your employer said it had none, or the authority reasonably believed your employer had failed to comply; from the day you said you would give further evidence to the day it was received, you said none would be given, or the authority reasonably believed none would be; and from the day the authority requested a further medical report it considered reasonable and necessary to the day it received the report. Empty if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day must my claim be determined?` `my claim is about` `the day my claim was received` `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` `the paused periods` MEANS
    `s 11A(1) -- the last day for determining my claim` `my claim is about` `the day my claim was received` `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` `the paused periods`

@export Has my claim for compensation been determined within the period the Regulations allow, or has that period run out (Act s 61(1A), reg s 11A(1))? Neither the Act nor the Regulations say what follows when the period is missed.
GIVEN `my claim is about` IS A `Kind of claim` @desc Is your claim about a disease (or the aggravation of a disease), or about another injury (or its aggravation)?
      `the day my claim was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the determining authority (Comcare or the licensee) received your claim. ISO 8601.
      `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your claim made in accordance with s 54 of the Act?
      `my claim has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the determining authority determined your claim?
      `the day it was determined` IS A DATE @desc If it has been determined, the day it was determined (ISO 8601); otherwise any date (it is not used).
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, or the day as at which you are asking (ISO 8601).
      `the paused periods` IS A LIST OF `Paused period` @desc Each period, first and last day inclusive (ISO 8601), in which days are not counted under reg s 11A(3) (a medical examination, a request for information to you or your employer, further evidence you said you would give, a further medical report). Empty if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where it stands`
`Was my claim determined in time?` `my claim is about` `the day my claim was received` `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` `my claim has been determined` `the day it was determined` `the day I am asking about` `the paused periods` MEANS
    `s 61(1A) -- where the determination of my claim stands` `my claim is about` `the day my claim was received` `my claim was made in accordance with s 54` `my claim has been determined` `the day it was determined` `the day I am asking about` `the paused periods`

@export I asked for a determination to be reconsidered: by what day must my request be decided (Act s 62(6), reg s 11A(2))? 30 calendar days, counting the day the request was received, for requests made on or after 1 April 2024. No period is prescribed for a request about a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38).
GIVEN `my request is for` IS A `Kind of request` @desc Is your request to reconsider a determination on your compensation claim (Act s 62), or a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)?
      `the day my request was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the determining authority received your request. ISO 8601.
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By what day must my request for reconsideration be decided?` `my request is for` `the day my request was received` MEANS
    `s 11A(2) -- the last day for deciding my request` `my request is for` `the day my request was received`

@export Has my request for reconsideration been decided within the 30 days the Regulations allow, or has that period run out (Act s 62(6), reg s 11A(2))?
GIVEN `my request is for` IS A `Kind of request` @desc Is your request to reconsider a determination on your compensation claim (Act s 62), or a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)?
      `the day my request was received` IS A DATE @desc The day the determining authority received your request. ISO 8601.
      `my request has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your request been decided?
      `the day it was decided` IS A DATE @desc If it has been decided, the day it was decided (ISO 8601); otherwise any date (it is not used).
      `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc Today's date, or the day as at which you are asking (ISO 8601).
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where it stands`
`Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `my request is for` `the day my request was received` `my request has been decided` `the day it was decided` `the day I am asking about` MEANS
    `s 62(6) -- where the decision on my request stands` `my request is for` `the day my request was received` `my request has been decided` `the day it was decided` `the day I am asking about`

§§ `My employer's licence was suspended or revoked (regs ss 18-31) -- for an employee of a licensee`

@export My employer was a Comcare licensee and its licence has been suspended or revoked: who is liable to pay my compensation (regs ss 19, 21, 27, 28)?
GIVEN `my employer is` IS A `Who held the licence` @desc Was your employer a Commonwealth authority (a licensed authority) or a corporation (a licensed corporation)?
      `what happened to the licence` IS A `What happened to the licence` @desc Was the licence suspended or revoked?
      `the licence covered accepting liability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the licence authorise your employer to accept liability to pay compensation to its employees?
      `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the licence was revoked: did your injury (or the loss, damage or death) occur before the day of revocation? For a suspension, answer yes.
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who is liable`
`Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `my employer is` `what happened to the licence` `the licence covered accepting liability` `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` MEANS
    `ss 19, 21, 27, 28 -- who is liable for my compensation`
        (`Licence facts` WITH
            `holder` IS `my employer is`
            `event` IS `what happened to the licence`
            `the licence covered accepting liability` IS `the licence covered accepting liability`
            `the licence covered managing claims` IS FALSE  -- not read by this rule
            `my injury occurred before the day of revocation` IS `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked`
            `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` IS FALSE  -- not read by this rule
            `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` IS FALSE)  -- not read by this rule

@export My employer was a Comcare licensee and its licence has been suspended or revoked: who manages my claim now (regs ss 19, 21, 27, 30)?
GIVEN `my employer is` IS A `Who held the licence` @desc Was your employer a Commonwealth authority (a licensed authority) or a corporation (a licensed corporation)?
      `what happened to the licence` IS A `What happened to the licence` @desc Was the licence suspended or revoked?
      `the licence covered managing claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the licence authorise your employer to manage its employees' claims?
      `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the licence was revoked: did your injury (or the loss, damage or death) occur before the day of revocation? For a suspension, answer yes.
      `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a corporation whose licence was revoked: has Comcare told you it has decided to manage your claim, or to arrange for another person to manage it (reg s 30(8))?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Who manages my claim`
`Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `my employer is` `what happened to the licence` `the licence covered managing claims` `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` MEANS
    `ss 19, 21, 27, 30 -- who manages my claim`
        (`Licence facts` WITH
            `holder` IS `my employer is`
            `event` IS `what happened to the licence`
            `the licence covered accepting liability` IS FALSE  -- not read by this rule
            `the licence covered managing claims` IS `the licence covered managing claims`
            `my injury occurred before the day of revocation` IS `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked`
            `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` IS `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management`
            `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` IS FALSE)  -- not read by this rule

@export If I give my claim, a notice or other communication to my employer after its licence was suspended or revoked, must my employer pass it on to Comcare (regs ss 19(3)(a)(iii), 21(3)(c)(i), 30(11)(a))?
GIVEN `my employer is` IS A `Who held the licence` @desc Was your employer a Commonwealth authority (a licensed authority) or a corporation (a licensed corporation)?
      `what happened to the licence` IS A `What happened to the licence` @desc Was the licence suspended or revoked?
      `the licence covered managing claims` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the licence authorise your employer to manage its employees' claims?
      `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the licence was revoked: did your injury occur before the day of revocation? For a suspension, answer yes.
      `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a corporation whose licence was revoked: has the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Commission demanded payment under the guarantee your employer gave for its liabilities (reg s 30(1))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `my employer is` `what happened to the licence` `the licence covered managing claims` `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked` `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` MEANS
    `ss 19, 21, 30 -- my employer must pass my claim to Comcare`
        (`Licence facts` WITH
            `holder` IS `my employer is`
            `event` IS `what happened to the licence`
            `the licence covered accepting liability` IS FALSE  -- not read by this rule
            `the licence covered managing claims` IS `the licence covered managing claims`
            `my injury occurred before the day of revocation` IS `my injury occurred before the day the licence was revoked`
            `Comcare has decided to manage my claim or arrange its management` IS FALSE  -- not read by this rule
            `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee` IS `the Commission has demanded payment under my employer's guarantee`)

@export My employer's Comcare licence was revoked: who is my rehabilitation authority (regs ss 22(1)(d), 25, 28(1)(d), 31)?
GIVEN `the preservation period has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission not yet determined the end of the preservation period for your former employer (the period runs from the day of revocation until the end day the Commission determines)?
      `Comcare has arranged another person to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Comcare arranged for another person to act as rehabilitation authority for your former employer's employees (reg s 25 or 31)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `My rehabilitation authority`
`Who is my rehabilitation authority after the licence was revoked?` `the preservation period has not ended` `Comcare has arranged another person to act` MEANS
    `ss 22, 28 -- my rehabilitation authority after revocation` `the preservation period has not ended` `Comcare has arranged another person to act`
